---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Waitlist from '../components/Waitlist.astro'
import { BMC_LINK, LINKS, SITE } from '../config'
---

<Base
  title={SITE.name}
  description="Agents that run your business out of numbered folders you can read, inside a layer that decides what they are allowed to touch. Start with 3 folders tonight, free."
  path="/"
>
  <section class="door">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="badge badge--accent">Hermes agents · ICM brains</span>
      <h1 class="door-title">Agents As Folders</h1>
      <p class="door-line">
        Agents that run your business out of folders you can read.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        Not a chatbot you re-explain yourself to every morning. Numbered
        folders hold the work, an agent walks them and does the job, and a
        layer above it decides what it is allowed to touch.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/start">Build 3 folders tonight</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/what-this-is/">What this actually is</a>
      </div>
      <p class="door-note">
        Free to start, nothing to install, about 20 minutes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="door-stack">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="door-n">01</span>
          <h2>Folders hold the work</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            Numbered, 1 job each. The number is the order the work happens in,
            not decoration. You can open any of them and read it yourself.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="door-n">02</span>
          <h2>An agent walks them</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            It reads the folder it is standing in and does that folder's job.
            Nobody re-explains the business to it in the morning.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="door-n">03</span>
          <h2>A layer above says no</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            What it can reach and what it can spend are handed to it from
            outside. It cannot widen them. Not because it promised, because it
            cannot.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>An app is a place to put things</h2>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">
        Notion is good software. Obsidian is good software. Neither one failed
        you. They are filing cabinets, and a filing cabinet is useful. It is
        just not a brain.
      </p>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">
        A brain gets walked. Something moves through it, picks up what it
        needs, and knows where to go next. That something is your AI. And here
        is the part nobody tells you: your AI does not browse. It does not get
        curious. It opens what you point it at.
      </p>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">
        So a beautiful vault means nothing to it if nothing tells it where to
        stand. You built a room with no doors.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>The fix is not another app.</strong> It is 3 folders with 3
          jobs, and an agent that reads the folder it is standing in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid" style="align-items:start">
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem">What it looks like</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted)">
            3 folders is enough to start. Each one holds 1 job and the notes
            for that job. Nothing else.
          </p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted)">
            Point your AI at <code
              style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--accent)">02_writing</code
            > and it already knows it is writing. Nobody had to explain that.
          </p>
        </div>
        <pre class="tree"><b>~/my-business/</b>
├── <b>01_research/</b>
│   ├── <i>customers.md</i>
│   └── <i>competitors.md</i>
├── <b>02_writing/</b>
│   ├── <i>how-i-write.md</i>
│   └── <i>offers.md</i>
└── <b>03_publishing/</b>
    ├── <i>where-it-goes.md</i>
    └── <i>checklist.md</i></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="badge">Free</span>
      <h2>Start with the free material</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        No card, no trial, no upsell wall. This is the part that should work
        before you pay anyone anything.
      </p>
      <div class="grid" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Hermes basics</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            Getting the agent running and pointed at a folder.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>ICM folder structures</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            How to number them, what goes inside, and when to add a 4th.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Automations</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            Cron jobs and scheduled work that runs without you watching.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Channels</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0">
            Wiring it into Discord, Telegram and email.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="where">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="badge">Where I teach</span>
      <h2>BuildMarketClose</h2>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">
        I am an admin in the BuildMarketClose community and I teach there. I am
        also building my own material inside it, in the open, as proof that
        their process works. If you want to watch that happen from the inside,
        that is where it is happening.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href={BMC_LINK} rel="sponsored noopener">
          Join BuildMarketClose
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="disclosure">
        Heads up: that is an affiliate link. I earn a commission if you join
        through it. I would point you there either way, because it is where I
        teach, but you should know before you click.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="vip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="badge">Not open yet</span>
      <h2>My VIP classroom</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Still in draft. You cannot buy it today and I am not going to pretend
        otherwise.
      </p>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">When it opens, it is where I put:</p>
      <ul style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        <li>My live Hermes setup. The real one, not a demo.</li>
        <li>My actual ICM folder structures, as I use them.</li>
        <li>Finished builds you can take and run.</li>
        <li>
          Request rights. You ask for a build, I make it, it lands in the
          classroom.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p style="max-width:40rem">
        The structured course material is being written now. It is not there
        yet. If you want a finished library today, wait for me. If you want to
        watch it get built and get in early, leave your email.
      </p>
      <Waitlist id="vip-waitlist" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Questions you are probably asking</h2>

      <h3>Is the free stuff actually free?</h3>
      <p style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        Yes. No card, no trial that converts, no locked lesson 4. The paid thing
        is separate and it is not open yet anyway.
      </p>

      <h3>What is the commission thing?</h3>
      <p style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        BuildMarketClose pays me if you join through my link. I teach there and
        I would recommend it regardless, but you deserve to know the incentive
        exists.
      </p>

      <h3>When does VIP open?</h3>
      <p style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        When the material is worth charging for. Leave your email and you will
        hear before anyone else.
      </p>

      <h3>Do I need to know how to code?</h3>
      <p style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        No. If you can make a folder and name it, you can do this. That is most
        of the point.
      </p>

      <h3>Is this just another second brain method?</h3>
      <p style="max-width:40rem;color:var(--muted)">
        Fair question. The difference is who it is built for. A second brain is
        usually built for you to read. This is built for your agent to walk, and
        that changes the shape of everything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <h2>Go make 3 folders tonight</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-inline:auto">
        Number them. Give each one a job. Then point your AI at one of them and
        watch it stop asking who you are.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center">
        <a class="btn" href="/start">Show me how</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={LINKS.youtube}>Watch on YouTube</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
